From: Claude (Anthropic AI) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nvapi: Enable D3D12 NV shader extensions by default.

The opt-in existed because vkd3d-proton dropped the NVAPI FP16/FP32 atomic
intrinsics, which broke titles that use them without querying support first
(Cyberpunk 2077). Those intrinsics are now translated, so flip the default.
DXVK_NVAPI_D3D12_NV_SHADER_EXTN=0 still forces it off.
---
--- a/src/util/util_env.cpp
+++ b/src/util/util_env.cpp
@@ -196,8 +196,12 @@
     bool isD3d12NvShaderExtnEnabled() {
         static bool alreadyLogged = false;
 
-        static bool enabled = getEnvVariable("DXVK_NVAPI_D3D12_NV_SHADER_EXTN") == "1"
-            || isNvidiaRtxPathTracingSample();
+        // Enabled by default: the vkd3d-proton side now implements the FP16x2
+        // and FP32 atomic intrinsics that used to be silently dropped, which was
+        // the reason this was kept behind an opt-in. Set the variable to 0 to
+        // force it off again.
+        auto override = getEnvVariable("DXVK_NVAPI_D3D12_NV_SHADER_EXTN");
+        static bool enabled = override != "0";
 
         if (enabled) {
             if (!std::exchange(alreadyLogged, true))
